---
# Two pools, not one. The ingress VIP has to be an address no ordinary LoadBalancer
# Service can take, and autoAssign: false is the only thing that actually enforces that —
# MetalLB will never hand this address out except to a Service that names it via the
# metallb.io/loadBalancerIPs annotation. A comment saying "don't use .240" would not
# survive the next service that asks for a LoadBalancer.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. `kubectl apply -f` processes documents in file order, and MetalLB's
# validating webhook rejects any pool overlapping an already-defined one. homelab-pool has to
# narrow FIRST: when this file was introduced it still covered 10.0.0.240-250, so applying
# ingress-pool ahead of it was denied with
#   CIDR "10.0.0.240/32" in pool "ingress-pool" overlaps with already defined CIDR "10.0.0.240/29"
# (MetalLB normalises the old range into CIDRs, and .240/29 is the first of them). Narrowing
# homelab-pool first makes the ingress /32 free by the time it is validated, on a fresh cluster
# and on the upgrade path alike.
apiVersion: metallb.io/v1beta1
kind: IPAddressPool
metadata:
  name: homelab-pool
  namespace: metallb-system
spec:
  addresses:
    - {{ k3s_metallb_pool }}
---
apiVersion: metallb.io/v1beta1
kind: IPAddressPool
metadata:
  name: ingress-pool
  namespace: metallb-system
spec:
  addresses:
    - {{ k3s_metallb_ingress_vip }}/32
  autoAssign: false
---
apiVersion: metallb.io/v1beta1
kind: L2Advertisement
metadata:
  name: homelab-l2
  namespace: metallb-system
spec:
  ipAddressPools:
    - ingress-pool
    - homelab-pool
  # Phase F join (2026-08-13): announce VIPs from daniel-box ONLY. Within minutes of the
  # join, daniel-server's speaker won the L2 election for 10.0.0.240 and every Docker
  # container on that host lost the cluster: a Docker-bridge client cannot reach a VIP
  # its own host announces (the hairpin class again — crowdsec agent, terraria-stats and
  # promtail all crash-looped on "dial tcp 10.0.0.240:443: i/o timeout" from 15:05).
  # PERMANENT (operator decision 2026-08-14, design.md §10 #6): with ETP Local load-bearing
  # for client-IP preservation and two asymmetric nodes, this pin and the VIP-backed
  # workloads' daniel-box nodeSelectors are one unit — never move either alone.
  #
  # THE FULL SET, because counting them was how two got missed: traefik, pihole, mosquitto,
  # terraria, valheim, wg-easy, and jellyfin. Valheim and wg-easy joined 2026-08-14 — both
  # had carried ETP Local and a VIP since going live with no pin at all, sitting on
  # daniel-box by scheduler accident. Jellyfin is the odd one out: it is pinned here by the
  # media-volume `local` PV's required nodeAffinity rather than by its own nodeSelector, so
  # jellyfin-lan's VIP is safe only for as long as that volume stays node-local.
  #
  # ANY NEW `type: LoadBalancer` SERVICE WITH externalTrafficPolicy: Local NEEDS A PIN HERE.
  # The failure is silent: the pod reports healthy on the wrong node while its VIP drops
  # every packet. `kubectl get svc -A | grep LoadBalancer` is the census.
  nodeSelectors:
    - matchLabels:
        kubernetes.io/hostname: daniel-box
